---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
import Related from '../../components/Related.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Gallery title="Pattern: inbox">
  <p class="demo-note">
    <strong>Who uses it</strong>: every ERP user, first thing — the screen a
    working day starts on. <strong>How often</strong>: continuously; it is
    the tab that stays open. <strong>What "done" looks like</strong>: the
    list is empty of things that need <em>you</em> — every row either acted
    on or explicitly handed off. An inbox is cross-type and cross-process:
    approvals, exceptions, assigned tasks and failed jobs in ONE list, and
    every row says <em>why it is yours</em>.
    <strong>Not for one document type's approval queue</strong> — that
    scoped, single-process view is the
    <a href={base + '/patterns/approval'}>approval workflow</a>'s job; and
    not a feed of things that merely <em>happened</em> — that is
    <a href={base + '/patterns/notification'}>notification</a>'s contract.
    The inbox holds only rows that block on a person.
  </p>
  <p class="demo-note">
    <strong>Routine approvals may decide in place.</strong> A single-step,
    unflagged approval row can expand to a compact preview — header facts,
    line summary, attachments — with Approve/Reject right there, running
    through <a href={base + '/patterns/approval'}>approval</a>'s own dialog
    and endpoints, never a second copy of them. Anything flagged, mid-chain,
    high-value, or not an approval keeps the plain link-out: a preview that
    can't show the real reason — an exception's diff, a job's log — is
    worse than the row it would replace.
  </p>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>The screen</h2>
    <div class="bo-cluster" style="margin-block-end: var(--bo-space-3)">
      <div class="bo-segmented" role="group" aria-label="Inbox filter">
        <input class="bo-segmented__input bo-visually-hidden" type="radio" name="inb-f" id="inb-all" checked>
        <label class="bo-segmented__option" for="inb-all">All (6)</label>
        <input class="bo-segmented__input bo-visually-hidden" type="radio" name="inb-f" id="inb-appr">
        <label class="bo-segmented__option" for="inb-appr">Approvals (3)</label>
        <input class="bo-segmented__input bo-visually-hidden" type="radio" name="inb-f" id="inb-exc">
        <label class="bo-segmented__option" for="inb-exc">Exceptions (2)</label>
        <input class="bo-segmented__input bo-visually-hidden" type="radio" name="inb-f" id="inb-task">
        <label class="bo-segmented__option" for="inb-task">Tasks (1)</label>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table">
        <caption class="bo-visually-hidden">Items needing your action</caption>
        <thead><tr>
          <th scope="col">Item</th>
          <th scope="col">Why it's yours</th>
          <th scope="col">Waiting</th>
          <th scope="col"><span class="bo-visually-hidden">Action</span></th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--type">PO</span> PO-88213 · Acme Supply Co. · $18,940.50</td>
            <td>Awaiting <strong>your approval</strong> — step 3 of 4</td>
            <td>2 days</td>
            <td><a class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--secondary" href={base + '/patterns/approval'}>Review</a></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--type">INV</span> INV-10236 · Initech GmbH · $730.25</td>
            <td><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--danger">Exception</span> price variance 12% over tolerance</td>
            <td>26 days</td>
            <td><a class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--secondary" href={base + '/patterns/object-page'}>Open</a></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--type">JOB</span> Nightly GR/IR reconciliation</td>
            <td><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--danger">Exception</span> failed at 02:14 — <strong>assigned to you</strong></td>
            <td>6 hours</td>
            <td><a class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--secondary" href={base + '/patterns/staging'}>Open log</a></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--type">PO</span> PO-88219 · Globex Industrial · $2,110.00</td>
            <td>Awaiting <strong>your approval</strong> — step 1 of 2</td>
            <td>4 hours</td>
            <td><a class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--secondary" href={base + '/patterns/approval'}>Review</a></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--type">TASK</span> Confirm vendor bank change · Stark Components</td>
            <td><strong>Assigned to you</strong> by J. Kim</td>
            <td>1 day</td>
            <td><a class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--secondary" href={base + '/patterns/record-detail'}>Open</a></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--type">REQ</span> Requisition R-4471 · Warehouse consumables</td>
            <td>Awaiting <strong>your approval</strong> — final step</td>
            <td>3 days</td>
            <td><button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--secondary" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="inb-r4471-detail">Preview</button></td>
          </tr>
          <tr id="inb-r4471-detail">
            <td colspan="4">
              <div class="bo-widget">
                <div class="bo-widget__body">
                  <dl class="bo-kv bo-kv--rows">
                    <div><dt>Requested by</dt><dd>T. Alvarez, Warehouse</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Cost centre</dt><dd>CC-3405</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Amount</dt><dd class="bo-amount">1,240.00 <span class="bo-amount__unit">USD</span></dd></div>
                  </dl>
                  <p class="bo-u-text-muted" style="margin-block: var(--bo-space-2) 0">
                    3 lines — nitrile gloves, air filters, degreaser ·
                    <a href="#">vendor-quote.pdf</a> (opens in a viewer, not inline —
                    a pane can't satisfy diligence on a scanned document)
                  </p>
                  <div class="bo-cluster" style="margin-block-start: var(--bo-space-3)">
                    <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm" type="button" data-dialog-trigger="inb-r4471-decide">Approve</button>
                    <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--danger" type="button" data-dialog-trigger="inb-r4471-decide">Reject</button>
                    <a class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--ghost" href={base + '/patterns/approval'}>Open full record</a>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Every row answers <em>why is this mine</em>
    in its own column — awaiting your approval, an exception assigned to
    you, a task handed to you — because a cross-type list without that
    column is just a worklist someone else has to explain. The 26-day row
    is deliberately old: <strong>age is the monitoring signal</strong>, and
    it must be visible without opening anything. <strong>PO-88213 stays
    link-out on purpose</strong> — deep in a 4-step chain and $18,940.50, it
    is exactly the case the ERP-practice review flagged for escalation, not
    a row we simply didn't get to. <strong>R-4471, above, is the opposite
    case</strong> — one step, one approver, modest value — shown expanded
    for illustration; the decision dialog itself is not in this static demo,
    same as <a href={base + '/patterns/approval'}>approval</a>'s own
    (<code>data-dialog-trigger</code> needs <code>initDialogs()</code>, and
    the toggle above needs its own small script to flip
    <code>aria-expanded</code> — this page has none, so both render
    permanently open here).</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>On a phone — one column, one action per row</h2>
    <div class="demo-phone-screen">
      <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
        <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Item</th>
              <th scope="col" class="bo-data-table__col--secondary">Waiting</th>
              <th scope="col" class="bo-data-table__col--tertiary">Source</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--warning">Approval</span> <a href={base + '/patterns/approval'}>PO-88213 · $48,200</a></td>
              <td class="bo-data-table__col--secondary bo-u-tabular">3d</td>
              <td class="bo-data-table__col--tertiary">Purchasing</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--danger">Exception</span> <a href={base + '/patterns/goods-receipt'}>GR-4471 short-shipped</a></td>
              <td class="bo-data-table__col--secondary bo-u-tabular">1d</td>
              <td class="bo-data-table__col--tertiary">Warehouse</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--type">Task</span> <a href={base + '/patterns/timesheet'}>Submit week 34</a></td>
              <td class="bo-data-table__col--secondary bo-u-tabular">6h</td>
              <td class="bo-data-table__col--tertiary">HR</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Same table, same rows — the
    <a href={base + '/components/data-table'}>column priority ladder</a>
    does the narrowing: Source (<code>--tertiary</code>) goes first, then
    Waiting (<code>--secondary</code>), and what survives is the one thing
    a phone reader needs — <strong>what it is and what it is about</strong>,
    as a link. Expand-in-place does not come along: a preview inside a
    390px row is a worse version of the screen it previews, so a phone row
    links out to <a href={base + '/patterns/approval'}>the decision
    screen</a>, which has its own phone section. Bulk claim is deliberately
    absent for the same reason approval drops its bulk queue.
    <strong>Not a mobile pattern</strong> — one inbox, read narrow.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Markup</h2>
    <pre><code>{`<!-- One list, many sources. The row's TYPE is a badge; the row's
     REASON is a column. Filter chips are a segmented control whose
     counts come from the server. -->
<div class="bo-segmented" role="group" aria-label="Inbox filter">
  <input class="bo-segmented__input bo-visually-hidden" type="radio"
         name="inb-f" id="inb-all" checked>
  <label class="bo-segmented__option" for="inb-all">All (6)</label>
  <!-- …one radio+label per row source -->
</div>

<table class="bo-data-table">
  <thead><tr>
    <th scope="col">Item</th>
    <th scope="col">Why it's yours</th>
    <th scope="col">Waiting</th>
    <th scope="col"><span class="bo-visually-hidden">Action</span></th>
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><span class="bo-badge bo-badge--type">PO</span> PO-88213 …</td>
      <td>Awaiting <strong>your approval</strong> — step 3 of 4</td>
      <td>2 days</td>
      <td><a class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--secondary"
             href="/approve/PO-88213">Review</a></td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>`}</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Anatomy</h2>
    <ol class="bo-stack bo-stack--tight docs-list">
      <li><strong>Filter chips</strong> — a
      <a href={base + '/components/segmented'}>segmented control</a>, one
      option per row source, counts rendered server-side. Native radios, so
      arrow keys move between filters for free.</li>
      <li><strong>The list</strong> — a plain
      <a href={base + '/components/data-table'}>data table</a>; each row's
      type is a <a href={base + '/components/badge'}>badge</a>, exceptions
      carry the danger tone <em>plus</em> the word (two-channel).</li>
      <li><strong>"Why it's yours" column</strong> — the inbox's defining
      part: <em>awaiting your approval</em> / <em>assigned to you</em> /
      <em>exception routed to you</em>. Bold on the phrase that names the
      reader.</li>
      <li><strong>Waiting column</strong> — age since the row became yours.
      This is the human-monitoring signal: an old row is visible shame,
      unopened.</li>
      <li><strong>Per-row action</strong> — one
      <a href={base + '/components/button'}>secondary button</a> linking
      into the screen that resolves the row (approval, object page, log).
      The inbox does not resolve rows itself, with one named exception
      below — everything else is still a link out, never a second decision
      surface.</li>
      <li><strong>Expand-in-place preview</strong> — a routine approval row
      only: a toggle button (<code>aria-expanded</code> /
      <code>aria-controls</code>) reveals <a href={base + '/components/kv'}>key-value
      facts</a> plus a line/attachment summary, with Approve/Reject wired to
      <a href={base + '/patterns/approval'}>approval</a>'s own decision
      dialog and endpoints — not a new dialog, not a new endpoint. Flagged,
      mid-chain, high-value, and every non-approval row keep the plain
      link-out; there is no generic "detail panel" here, because the four
      row types share no common shape to hang one on.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Data contract</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Request</th><th scope="col">Returns / on failure</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">GET /inbox?filter=approvals</td><td>the tbody fragment + refreshed chip counts; an agent reads the same rows the human sees — <code>data-item-id</code>, <code>data-reason</code>, <code>data-age-hours</code> per row make it machine-readable without scraping prose</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">POST /inbox/:id/claim</td><td>the row re-rendered as claimed (byline: who); 409 if someone claimed it first — re-render with the claimer's name, never silently drop</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">resolution</td><td>happens on the TARGET screen (approve on the approval screen, fix on the object page); the inbox row disappears on the next fetch — the inbox never posts a decision itself, with one exception below</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="bo-data-table__col--code">POST /req/:id/approve<br>POST /req/:id/reject</td><td><strong>the one exception</strong>: a routine, single-remaining-step approval row's expanded preview posts here directly — this is <a href={base + '/patterns/approval'}>approval</a>'s own decision contract, reused verbatim (reject's reason is REQUIRED server-side, 409 if already decided → re-render naming who decided), reached through approval's own dialog. No new inbox-owned decision endpoint exists for any row type</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted"><strong>The AI-manages / human-monitors
    split, stated</strong>: an agent works this screen through the row data
    attributes and the claim/resolve endpoints; the human monitors through
    the chip counts, the danger badges, and the Waiting column. Same rows,
    two channels — neither is decoration.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>States</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">What ships</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Nothing needs you</td><td><strong>a success, and it must look like one</strong> — "Inbox zero · nothing is waiting on you" with a positive tone, never the same grey empty-box as a filter mismatch</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Filtered to empty</td><td>the DIFFERENT empty: "No exceptions right now — 4 items under other filters", with the chips still showing their counts so the reader knows where the work went</td></tr>
          <tr><td>New rows arrived</td><td>chip counts update on the next poll; rows the reader has scrolled past are never reordered under them mid-read</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Claimed by a colleague</td><td>409 on claim → the row re-renders naming the claimer; it leaves the list on the next fetch</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Row's document deleted</td><td>the row states it plainly ("PO-88213 no longer exists") with a dismiss — a dead link that 404s is a support call</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Overdue</td><td>the Waiting cell past a threshold gains the warning tone + the word "overdue" — two channels, and the age was already visible before the threshold</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Approval row, expanded</td><td>header facts, line summary, and an attachment list render inline; the attachment itself never does — it opens in a dedicated viewer, since a preview pane can't carry the diligence a scanned document or PDF needs</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Approval row, escalated</td><td>flagged, mid-chain, or high-value stays a plain link-out row — no preview button at all, so there is nothing that looks decidable but isn't</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Decision submitted from the preview</td><td>same as approval's own: dialog buttons disabled until the swap lands, so a failed note is never lost; success re-renders the row gone (it resolved) or, on 409, re-renders the preview naming who decided first</td></tr>
          <tr><td>On a phone</td><td>the priority ladder leaves item + link; expand-in-place is not offered at all, so no row looks decidable in place when it isn't — the row links out to approval's phone decision card</td></tr>
          <tr><td>No JS</td><td>the base list is fully functional with no JS dependency — filter chips are native radios, rows are a plain table, every link-out action is an ordinary link, and the polling/claim/409 behaviour above is the server's job, not client script. <strong>Stated honestly, not papered over</strong>: the expand-in-place toggle (<code>aria-expanded</code>) and the decision dialog both need JS, the same as approval's own dialog does on its own page — without it, a routine row simply keeps its plain link-out, same as every other row</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Components used</h2>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted"><span class="bo-badge">complexity 2 of 4</span></p>
    <ul class="bo-cluster docs-list-bare">
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/data-table'}>Data table</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/segmented'}>Segmented control</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/badge'}>Badge</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/button'}>Button</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/kv'}>Key-value facts</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <Related links={[
    ["/patterns/approval", "Approval workflow"],
    ["/patterns/bulk-actions", "Bulk actions"],
    ["/patterns/kanban", "Kanban board (status as columns, when stage matters more than a queue)"],
    ["/patterns/list-report", "List report"],
    ["/components/data-table", "Data table"],
  ]} />
</Gallery>
